From 7a5f1c89abe8f388e9c3d8d4c9870b93364f032a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:41:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 011/109] Input: add Spreadtrum SC8830 keypad; gtelwifi:
 hardware keys

New driver for the keypad matrix controller of the SC8830/SC7730: up
to 8x8, four key slots in KEY_STATUS with press/release interrupt bits
per slot. Only rows and columns used by linux,keymap are scanned, the
other keypad pads may be muxed to GPIO and float. Home and Volume Up
of the gtelwifi sit on it.

Power and Volume Down are inputs of the SC2723 PMIC EIC block behind
the ADI bus. Until the sc27xx MFD supports the SC2723, expose them as
a polled GPIO chip (mach-sprd/pmic-eic.c) for gpio-keys-polled.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
---
